    "quotation": {
     "value": "The general accordance of M. LE VERRIER's results respecting the mass and orbit of the unknown planet with those of Mr. ADAMS, previously known to me, inspired renewed confidence in the theoretical deductions, and induced me to alter my plan of operations. On the evening of September 29, I swept over a considerable breadth in declination, within the limits of longitude marked out by M. LE VERRIER, resolving, if possible, to include the planet. The night was a good one; I observed without intermission three hours and a half, and recorded the positions of nearly 300 stars, paying more particular attention to the physical appearance of the brighter stars. One only attracted my attention, against which I directed my assistant to note, \"It seems to have a disk.\"",
